---
import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import { tools } from '../data/tools';
---

<Layout
  pageTitle="Tooliva — 25+ Free Online Developer Tools | JSON, JWT, Regex & More"
  pageDescription="25+ free online developer tools — JSON formatter, JWT decoder, regex tester, diff checker, hash generator, CSS minifier & more. Fast, private, client-side utilities."
  pageKeywords="json formatter, json formatter online, jwt decoder, regex tester online, diff checker, hash generator, css minifier, html minifier, base64 encoder, uuid generator, cron builder, color converter, password generator, developer tools online, free developer tools"
>
  <section class="hero-band">
    <div class="mesh-gradient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="grid-pattern" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="grain-overlay" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    <div class="floating-elements" aria-hidden="true">
      <span class="float-el el-1">&#123;&#125;</span>
      <span class="float-el el-2">[ ]</span>
      <span class="float-el el-3">&lt;/&gt;</span>
      <span class="float-el el-4">=&gt;</span>
      <span class="float-el el-5">/**</span>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-content">
      <span class="badge-pill">
        <span class="pill-static">Tools &middot; Utility &middot;</span>
        <span class="pill-rotating-wrap" id="rotating-wrap">
          <span class="pill-rotating" id="rotating-text"></span>
        </span>
        <span class="pill-tag">&lt;Utility /&gt;</span>
      </span>
      <h1 class="hero-title">
        Developer tools, done <span class="highlight-word">right</span>.
      </h1>
      <p class="hero-subtitle">The tools you Google &mdash; but fast, clean, and instant.</p>
      <div class="hero-cta">
        <a href="/tools" class="btn-primary">Get Started</a>
        <a href="/about" class="btn-secondary">Learn More</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="tools-band fade-in">
    <div class="tools-container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Every tool you need.</h2>
      <p class="section-subtitle">
        Quick, reliable utilities for developers &mdash; no fuss, just speed.
      </p>

      <div class="tools-grid">
        {
          tools.map((tool) => (
            <ToolCard
              name={tool.name}
              slug={tool.slug}
              description={tool.description}
              category={tool.category}
            />
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="seo-content-band fade-in">
    <div class="seo-content-container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Free Online Developer Tools for Every Workflow</h2>

      <div class="seo-content-grid">
        <article class="seo-content-block">
          <h3 class="seo-content-heading">
            JSON Formatter & Code Utilities — Format, Validate & Minify
          </h3>
          <p>
            Working with JSON data is a daily necessity for modern developers. Tooliva offers the
            best free <strong>JSON formatter online</strong> — a powerful tool that instantly formats,
            validates, and beautifies your JSON data with proper indentation. Our <strong
              >free online JSON formatter</strong
            > acts as a full <strong>JSON validator</strong> and <strong>JSON parser</strong>,
            catching syntax errors before they cause problems in your application. Unlike other
            tools that send your data to a server, everything runs client-side. Your data never
            leaves your browser.
          </p>
          <p>
            Beyond JSON, we provide a complete suite of code utilities. Our <strong
              >HTML minifier</strong
            >, <strong>CSS minifier</strong>, and <strong>JavaScript minifier</strong> strip whitespace
            and comments from your code, reducing file sizes for production. The <strong
              >SQL formatter</strong
            > beautifies your database queries, while the <strong>Markdown preview</strong> lets you write
            and preview rendered HTML side by side. Use our <strong>HTML entity converter</strong> to
            encode and decode special characters. Whether you need a <strong>JSON beautifier</strong
            >, <strong>JSON lint</strong> checker, or <strong>JSON viewer</strong>, Tooliva is your
            one-stop destination for code formatting tools.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="seo-content-block">
          <h3 class="seo-content-heading">
            Security & Text Tools — JWT Decoder, Hash Generator & Regex Tester
          </h3>
          <p>
            JSON Web Tokens are the backbone of modern authentication. Tooliva's <strong
              >JWT decoder</strong
            > instantly parses the header, payload, and signature sections of any RFC 7519 compliant token,
            presenting the data in a clean, structured format. Unlike many <strong
              >JWT parser</strong
            > tools that require server-side processing, our decoder runs entirely in your browser, ensuring
            sensitive token data never touches a network. It works perfectly as a drop-in replacement
            for jwt.io when you need a fast, private <strong>JWT decoder online</strong>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Our security toolkit also includes a <strong>hash generator</strong> supporting MD5, SHA-1,
            SHA-256, and SHA-512 using the Web Crypto API, and a <strong>password generator</strong> that
            creates strong random passwords with configurable length, character types, and entropy strength
            indicator. For text processing, the <strong>regex tester</strong> lets you test regular expressions
            with live matching across multi-line strings, and the <strong>diff checker</strong> compares
            two texts side by side using an LCS-based algorithm with color-coded additions and removals.
            The <strong>text replacer</strong> supports find-and-replace with optional regex mode.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="seo-content-block">
          <h3 class="seo-content-heading">Encoding, Conversion & Design Tools for Developers</h3>
          <p>
            Tooliva offers a comprehensive set of encoding and conversion utilities. Our <strong
              >Base64 encoder and decoder</strong
            > lets you encode strings and decode Base64 data instantly, with an optional URL-safe mode.
            The <strong>URL encoder/decoder</strong> handles percent-encoding for query parameters and
            full URLs. Generate unique identifiers with our <strong>UUID generator</strong>,
            supporting v4 (random) and v1 (time-based) with bulk generation up to 100 UUIDs at once.
            The <strong>JSON to CSV converter</strong> transforms JSON arrays to CSV and back, while the
            <strong>HTML entity converter</strong> handles both named and numeric character references.
          </p>
          <p>
            For designers and frontend developers, the <strong>color converter</strong> translates between
            HEX, RGB, and HSL color spaces with a live preview. The <strong
              >CSS gradient generator</strong
            > provides a visual builder for linear and radial gradients, outputting ready-to-use CSS code.
            The <strong>number base converter</strong> converts between binary, octal, decimal, and hexadecimal.
            Build and understand cron schedules with the <strong>cron builder</strong> — perfect for DevOps
            engineers managing scheduled tasks. Round out your workflow with the <strong
              >case converter</strong
            >, <strong>timestamp converter</strong>, <strong>lorem ipsum generator</strong>, and <strong
              >word counter</strong
            >. All tools are free, private, and require no account setup.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="features-band fade-in">
    <div class="features-container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Why Tooliva?</h2>
      <div class="features-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#123;&#125;</div>
          <h3 class="feature-title">Blazing Fast</h3>
          <p class="feature-text">
            Tools load instantly and process data in your browser. No server calls, no waiting.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#128274;</div>
          <h3 class="feature-title">Privacy First</h3>
          <p class="feature-text">
            Everything runs client-side. Your data never leaves your device. Period.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="feature-icon">&#9889;</div>
          <h3 class="feature-title">Zero Setup</h3>
          <p class="feature-text">
            No accounts, no sign-ups, no subscriptions. Open a tool and use it immediately.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-band fade-in">
    <div class="faq-container">
      <h2 class="section-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Is Tooliva free?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Yes, every tool is completely free to use. There are no hidden charges, premium tiers,
            or usage limits. All <strong>free online developer tools</strong> on Tooliva are available
            to everyone without any cost.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">How does the JSON formatter work?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Our <strong>JSON formatter online</strong> parses and pretty-prints your JSON data entirely
            in your browser. Paste or type your JSON, and it instantly formats with proper indentation.
            It also validates your JSON syntax and highlights errors, acting as both a <strong
              >JSON validator</strong
            > and <strong>JSON beautifier</strong> in one tool.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Is the JWT decoder safe to use with real tokens?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Absolutely. The <strong>JWT decoder online</strong> runs entirely client-side. Your token
            never leaves your browser, so sensitive authentication data stays private. Use it confidently
            as your go-to <strong>JWT token decoder</strong> for debugging production tokens.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Do I need an account?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            No. Just open a tool and start using it. There is no registration, no email sign-up, and
            no data collection. That's what makes Tooliva the <strong>best JSON formatter</strong> and
            developer tools platform for privacy-conscious users.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Is my data safe?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Yes. All tools run in your browser using client-side JavaScript. Your data never leaves
            your device. We don't store, log, or transmit any information you paste into our tools.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Can I use these tools offline?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Once a tool page loads, it works without an internet connection. All processing is done
            locally in your browser, making our <strong>pretty JSON formatter</strong> and other utilities
            fully functional offline.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">
            What is the difference between JSON format, validate, and beautify?
          </h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Formatting applies consistent indentation to raw JSON. Validation checks if your JSON
            follows proper syntax rules. Beautifying (or pretty printing) is the same as formatting
            — making compressed JSON human-readable. Tooliva's <strong
              >free online JSON formatter</strong
            > does all three simultaneously.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">How does the Diff Checker work?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Our <strong>diff checker</strong> uses an LCS (Longest Common Subsequence) algorithm to compare
            two texts line by line. Added lines are highlighted in green, removed lines in red, and unchanged
            lines in neutral. It handles texts of any size and works entirely in your browser.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Is the Hash Generator secure?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Yes. The <strong>hash generator</strong> uses the Web Crypto API (SubtleCrypto) built into
            modern browsers — the same cryptographic primitive used for HTTPS. It supports MD5, SHA-1,
            SHA-256, and SHA-512. All processing happens locally on your device.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">How many tools does Tooliva have?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            Tooliva currently offers <strong>25 free online developer tools</strong> across categories
            including code formatting, text processing, security, encoding, design, and DevOps. We're
            actively adding more utilities based on developer feedback.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-item">
          <h3 class="faq-question">Are more tools coming?</h3>
          <p class="faq-answer">
            We're building new utilities regularly. Our goal is to become the most comprehensive
            collection of <strong>free online developer tools</strong> on the web. Suggestions are always
            welcome.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  const words = ['JSON', 'Regex', 'Diff', 'Minify', 'Hash', 'Convert', 'Encode', 'Format'];
  const el = document.getElementById('rotating-text')!;
  let index = 0;

  function cycleWord() {
    index = (index + 1) % words.length;
    const currentOffset = -(index * 1.3);
    el.style.transform = `translateY(${currentOffset}em)`;
  }

  for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
    const span = document.createElement('span');
    span.textContent = words[i];
    el.appendChild(span);
  }
  el.style.transform = 'translateY(0)';

  setInterval(cycleWord, 2800);
</script>
